  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STEM Education for 25 Women Youth in South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will provide Technical Information Technology training to educate and empower 25 young women from South African townships and informal settlements. They will graduate as Professional Computer Support Technicians and System Engineers with skills to service and repair computers, printers, mobile phones and other hand-held devices. By providing technical skills, the project will open doors to both employment or self-employment opportunities for young women in a field dominated by men.</narrative>
  </description>
